# Auto-generated by secrets.sh — do not edit manually.
#
# Empty by default so the stack works in env-only mode: every service's
# `${..._PASSWORD_FILE:-}` resolves to blank (so postgres/keycloak read
# the plain `POSTGRES_PASSWORD`/`KC_DB_PASSWORD` env vars from .env),
# and every top-level `${..._SOURCE:-./secrets/.placeholder}` falls back
# to the tracked empty `docker/secrets/.placeholder` bind-mount.
#
# `secrets.sh` overwrites this file locally when the operator opts into
# the docker/secrets/*.txt pipeline — it emits the `_FILE=/run/secrets/*`
# indirection vars plus one `<KEY>_SOURCE=./secrets/<key>.txt` line per
# real secret, and blanks POSTGRES_PASSWORD / KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_PASSWORD /
# KC_DB_PASSWORD so the `_FILE` variants win. That local write is
# expected; do not commit it.
